  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Authentication Process Modification — /etc/pam.d/sshd Changed", "technique": "T1556.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-04-30 14:02:14 CEST, Wazuh FIM on ubuntu-app-srv-12 (agent.id=212) reported syscheck.event='modified' on syscheck.path=/etc/pam.d/sshd, syscheck.uname_after='root'. The diff added one line: 'auth required pam_duo.so' inserted above '@include common-auth'. The Wazuh correlation rule 550 fired with rule.mitre.id=T1556.003 because ANY write to /etc/pam.d/ is treated as Tier-0 sensitive activity and surfaced to the SOC for review.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 550 'Integrity checksum changed: /etc/pam.d/sshd' fires on every change to PAM files regardless of authorization status. Severity 'high' is set on the asset class — every PAM change must be human-reviewed. The rule firing does NOT presume malicious intent.", "first_seen": "2026-04-30T14:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Concurrent Ansible Job Execution from corp-ansible-tower-01", "technique": "context", "what_happened": "At 14:01:57 CEST (17 seconds BEFORE the PAM modification), Linux auditd on ubuntu-app-srv-12 captured an SSH session from corp-ansible-tower-01 (10.108.50.55) as data.audit.user='svc_ansible' (uid=998 — the documented Ansible Tower service account). The SSH key fingerprint matches the corp-ansible-tower-01 host key in the corp known_hosts repository. Within the same SSH session at 14:02:11, data.audit.exe=/usr/bin/dpkg-query with data.audit.command='dpkg-query -W duo*' returned 'duo-unix 1.12.0-1corp' — confirming the legitimate corp Duo package is already installed (vendor-signed, from the corp apt repository). The PAM modification at 14:02:14 traces to data.audit.exe=/usr/bin/sed editing /etc/pam.d/sshd as part of the Ansible role tasks. The session also carries an environment variable AWX_JOB_ID=4421 and AWX_TEMPLATE_NAME='corp.duo-rollout'.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh's auditd integration captures the SSH session metadata + the EXECVE chain. The data.audit.user='svc_ansible' + AWX_JOB_ID=4421 environment marker matches the corp Ansible Tower job tracking — every Ansible Tower task injects the AWX job ID into the executing user's environment.", "first_seen": "2026-04-30T14:01:57+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Vendor-Signed Package + Approved Change Ticket Context", "technique": "context", "what_happened": "The dpkg-query output captured in step 2 shows 'duo-unix 1.12.0-1corp'. The package origin is the corp internal apt repository which mirrors the upstream Duo Security signed Debian packages. The corp ServiceNow change-management system has an APPROVED change ticket CHG-2026-04-30-9 with subject 'Corp Duo 2FA rollout phase 2 — application servers tier' covering the change window 14:00-15:00 CEST 2026-04-30. Approver: corp Security Architecture Board, approved 2026-04-29 10:14 CEST. The ticket lists the target server list (including ubuntu-app-srv-12), the Ansible role version (corp.duo v1.12), and the expected PAM stanza diff (the literal 'auth required pam_duo.so' line that Q1's syscheck.diff will show).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh enriches the rule-550 PAM-change event with the matching ServiceNow change-ticket via the integrated change-management correlator. Match score: change_ticket=CHG-2026-04-30-9 + change_window 14:00-15:00 + activity_time 14:02:14 = INSIDE_WINDOW + target_host=ubuntu-app-srv-12 IN change_ticket.affected_hosts.", "first_seen": "2026-04-30T14:02:14+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "PAM Stanza Static Safety Check", "technique": "context", "what_happened": "The injected line is literally 'auth required pam_duo.so' — the canonical Duo Security PAM integration. There is NO pam_exec.so (the malicious pattern), NO nullok option (which would weaken the check), NO external script path (no reference to /tmp/, /var/tmp/, /usr/local/bin/, or any user home), NO hidden-dot-prefix filename, NO download cradle (no curl/wget/python). The 'required' control flow means the auth step MUST succeed (the OPPOSITE of an attacker pattern, which typically uses 'optional' or 'sufficient' to avoid breaking legitimate logins while still capturing credentials).", "chain_reason": "Static safety scan rule 80715 'PAM stanza added without risky markers' fired as INFORMATIONAL with rule.mitre.id=null — the scan checked the syscheck.diff content for the standard malicious-PAM signature set (pam_exec, nullok, expose_authtok with external path, hidden-dot-prefix script paths) and found none.", "first_seen": "2026-04-30T14:02:14+0200"}
  ],
